learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-28T10:34:42.034Z","harness:claude-code","A gate that is opt-in via a manifest field is only as strong as the code path that reads the field. Here the field is read — and then overridden by a capability check that runs first, so the declaration is inert for exactly the extensions that most need it. The general check: when a config field is supposed to narrow behaviour, find the branch that returns the broad answer and confirm the narrow branch is evaluated before it, not after. Reading the parser alone would have shown the field being parsed correctly.\n\nThe proof that mattered was not source reading but the shipped scaffold: generate the artifact the product tells authors to generate, install it, and observe whether the runtime honours what it emitted. `pm extension --init --capability renderers` produces a manifest declaring a narrow scope, and `pm list --limit 1 --profile` shows that extension loaded anyway. One command each way, and it cannot be argued with."
body: ""
